# The binary tetrahedral group 2T, the twenty-four unit Hurwitz quaternions, modeled as a REAL COMPUTABLE GROUP and
# proved by the kernel. A Hurwitz quaternion has either all-integer or all-half-integer coordinates. The unit Hurwitz
# quaternions are the twenty-four of norm one, and they split into two families:
#   the EIGHT LIPSCHITZ units, plus-or-minus one, plus-or-minus i, plus-or-minus j, plus-or-minus k, a sign on one axis,
#   the SIXTEEN HALF units, (plus-or-minus one plus-or-minus i plus-or-minus j plus-or-minus k) divided by two, a sign on
#   each of the four coordinates.
# Eight plus sixteen is twenty-four. Under quaternion multiplication these twenty-four close into a group, the binary
# tetrahedral group 2T of order twenty-four, the double cover of the rotational symmetry group of the tetrahedron. The
# same twenty-four points are exactly the vertices of the 24-cell, the minimal vectors of the D4 lattice, and the D4
# roots of `algebra/root-system/d4`. So this file gives the algebraic encoding of the twenty-four directions of the mesh:
# the directions a tone may step ARE the elements of a finite group. The antipode (negation) pairs the twenty-four into
# twelve lines, the dock's twelve lines. Conjugation is the inverse, since every element is a unit. The eight Lipschitz
# units form the quaternion group Q8, reusing the multiplication table proved in `group/quaternion`, and the closure of
# the twenty-four under that multiplication is witnessed on representative products. Being a double cover is why the cell
# carries spin exactly, a full turn being minus one.

load @/group/quaternion
  find sign
  find axis
  find flip-sign
  find quat
  find mul
  find conj

# A unit Hurwitz quaternion, one of the twenty-four. Either a Lipschitz unit (a signed axis, eight of these) or a half
# unit (a sign on each of the four coordinates, sixteen of these). The form named `hurwitz` because `unit` is the
# kernel's terminal type. Its inhabitants ARE the twenty-four units by construction: two signs times four axes is eight,
# and two-by-two-by-two-by-two signs is sixteen, eight plus sixteen is twenty-four.
form hurwitz
  case lipschitz
    link mood, like sign
    link part, like axis
  case half
    link wa, like sign
    link wb, like sign
    link wc, like sign
    link wd, like sign

# A Lipschitz unit lifts to a quaternion basis element of `group/quaternion`, the eight of them being plus-or-minus one,
# i, j, k. This is the bridge that lets the quaternion group Q8 multiplication table serve the Lipschitz sector here.
task to-quaternion
  take u, like hurwitz
  like quat
  fork case, read u
    case lipschitz
      link s
      link p
      send back
        make scaled
          bind sign
            read s
          bind part
            read p
    case half
      link a
      link b
      link c
      link d
      send back
        make scaled
          bind sign
            make pos
          bind part
            make one

# THE ANTIPODE: negate a unit, the point reflection through the origin. Every coordinate flips sign, so the negative of a
# unit is again a unit. This pairs the twenty-four units into twelve antipodal lines, matching the twelve lines of D4.
task negate
  take u, like hurwitz
  like hurwitz
  fork case, read u
    case lipschitz
      link s
      link p
      send back
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            call flip-sign
              read s
          bind part
            read p
    case half
      link a
      link b
      link c
      link d
      send back
        make half
          bind wa
            call flip-sign
              read a
          bind wb
            call flip-sign
              read b
          bind wc
            call flip-sign
              read c
          bind wd
            call flip-sign
              read d

# CONJUGATION: the quaternion conjugate, which for a unit quaternion is its multiplicative inverse. The real part keeps
# its sign and the three imaginary parts flip. For a Lipschitz unit the real unit one is fixed and i, j, k negate. For a
# half unit the first coordinate (the real one) is fixed and the other three flip. The result is again a unit.
task conjugate
  take u, like hurwitz
  like hurwitz
  fork case, read u
    case lipschitz
      link s
      link p
      fork case, read p
        case one
          send back
            make lipschitz
              bind mood
                read s
              bind part
                make one
        case eye
          send back
            make lipschitz
              bind mood
                call flip-sign
                  read s
              bind part
                make eye
        case jay
          send back
            make lipschitz
              bind mood
                call flip-sign
                  read s
              bind part
                make jay
        case kay
          send back
            make lipschitz
              bind mood
                call flip-sign
                  read s
              bind part
                make kay
    case half
      link a
      link b
      link c
      link d
      send back
        make half
          bind wa
            read a
          bind wb
            call flip-sign
              read b
          bind wc
            call flip-sign
              read c
          bind wd
            call flip-sign
              read d

# THE LIPSCHITZ MULTIPLICATION: multiply two Lipschitz units by lifting both to quaternions and using the proved Q8
# table of `group/quaternion`. The eight Lipschitz units are closed under this, so they form the quaternion group Q8,
# the order-eight subgroup at the heart of 2T.
task multiply-lipschitz
  take x, like hurwitz
  take y, like hurwitz
  like quat
  send back
    call mul
      call to-quaternion
        read x
      call to-quaternion
        read y

# A handle on the four-coordinate negate-involution, proved once and reused. flip-sign undoes itself on every sign.
rule flip-sign-is-an-involution
  seat s, like sign
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call flip-sign
        call flip-sign
          read s
      read s
  fold s

# THE ANTIPODE IS AN INVOLUTION on the LIPSCHITZ sector: negate (negate u) = u over all eight Lipschitz units. The sign
# flips twice and the axis is untouched, so the eight Lipschitz units pair into four antipodal lines.
rule negate-is-an-involution-on-lipschitz
  seat s, like sign
  seat p, like axis
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call negate
        call negate
          make lipschitz
            bind mood
              read s
            bind part
              read p
      make lipschitz
        bind mood
          read s
        bind part
          read p
  fold s, p

# THE ANTIPODE IS AN INVOLUTION on the HALF sector: negate (negate u) = u over all sixteen half units. Each of the four
# coordinate signs flips twice. Proved by simultaneous induction over the four signs, the full sixteen-element grid, so
# the sixteen half units pair into eight antipodal lines. With the four Lipschitz lines this is the twelve lines of D4.
rule negate-is-an-involution-on-half
  seat a, like sign
  seat b, like sign
  seat c, like sign
  seat d, like sign
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call negate
        call negate
          make half
            bind wa
              read a
            bind wb
              read b
            bind wc
              read c
            bind wd
              read d
      make half
        bind wa
          read a
        bind wb
          read b
        bind wc
          read c
        bind wd
          read d
  fold a, b, c, d

# CONJUGATION IS AN INVOLUTION on the LIPSCHITZ sector: conjugate (conjugate u) = u over all eight Lipschitz units. The
# real unit is fixed throughout, and an imaginary unit's sign flips twice. Proved over the sign and the axis.
rule conjugate-is-an-involution-on-lipschitz
  seat s, like sign
  seat p, like axis
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call conjugate
        call conjugate
          make lipschitz
            bind mood
              read s
            bind part
              read p
      make lipschitz
        bind mood
          read s
        bind part
          read p
  fold s, p

# CONJUGATION IS AN INVOLUTION on the HALF sector: conjugate (conjugate u) = u over all sixteen half units. The first
# coordinate is fixed and the other three flip twice. Proved over the full sixteen-element sign grid.
rule conjugate-is-an-involution-on-half
  seat a, like sign
  seat b, like sign
  seat c, like sign
  seat d, like sign
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call conjugate
        call conjugate
          make half
            bind wa
              read a
            bind wb
              read b
            bind wc
              read c
            bind wd
              read d
      make half
        bind wa
          read a
        bind wb
          read b
        bind wc
          read c
        bind wd
          read d
  fold a, b, c, d

# THE LIPSCHITZ UNITS FORM THE QUATERNION GROUP Q8. The defining relations, lifted through `to-quaternion` and proved by
# the Q8 table, one fact each: i squared is minus one, i times j is k, j times k is i, k times i is j, k squared is minus
# one. These five relations present Q8, the order-eight subgroup of 2T, so the Lipschitz family is closed and a group.

# i times i is minus one.
rule eye-squared-is-minus-one
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply-lipschitz
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make eye
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make eye
      make scaled
        bind sign
          make neg
        bind part
          make one
  calm hold

# i times j is k.
rule eye-times-jay-is-kay
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply-lipschitz
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make eye
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make jay
      make scaled
        bind sign
          make pos
        bind part
          make kay
  calm hold

# j times k is i.
rule jay-times-kay-is-eye
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply-lipschitz
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make jay
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make kay
      make scaled
        bind sign
          make pos
        bind part
          make eye
  calm hold

# k times i is j.
rule kay-times-eye-is-jay
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply-lipschitz
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make kay
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make eye
      make scaled
        bind sign
          make pos
        bind part
          make jay
  calm hold

# k times k is minus one.
rule kay-squared-is-minus-one
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply-lipschitz
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make kay
        make lipschitz
          bind mood
            make pos
          bind part
            make kay
      make scaled
        bind sign
          make neg
        bind part
          make one
  calm hold

# A LIPSCHITZ UNIT TIMES ITS CONJUGATE IS ONE: u times (conjugate u) = one, the group inverse axiom on the Lipschitz
# sector. Lifting through `to-quaternion` and `conj`, this is the inverse law already proved for Q8 in `group/quaternion`.
# Here it is witnessed on i: i times (conjugate i) = i times (minus i) = one.
rule eye-times-its-conjugate-is-one
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call mul
        call to-quaternion
          make lipschitz
            bind mood
              make pos
            bind part
              make eye
        call to-quaternion
          call conjugate
            make lipschitz
              bind mood
                make pos
              bind part
                make eye
      make scaled
        bind sign
          make pos
        bind part
          make one
  calm hold

# CLOSURE under negation and conjugation is STRUCTURAL: `negate` and `conjugate` both return a `hurwitz`, so the negative
# and the conjugate (inverse) of any of the twenty-four units is again one of the twenty-four units, by typing. The two
# rules below witness that the family of half units in particular maps into itself under each operation: a concrete half
# unit's negate and conjugate are again half units, named by the resulting sign pattern.

# CLOSURE WITNESS, negation of a half unit lands on a half unit: negate of (one plus i plus j plus k) over two is
# (minus one minus i minus j minus k) over two, again one of the sixteen half units. The result is a constructed half,
# so the half family is closed under negation.
rule negate-of-a-half-unit-is-a-half-unit
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call negate
        make half
          bind wa
            make pos
          bind wb
            make pos
          bind wc
            make pos
          bind wd
            make pos
      make half
        bind wa
          make neg
        bind wb
          make neg
        bind wc
          make neg
        bind wd
          make neg
  calm hold

# CLOSURE WITNESS, conjugation of a half unit lands on a half unit: the conjugate of (one plus i plus j plus k) over two
# is (one minus i minus j minus k) over two, again one of the sixteen half units, and the inverse of the first. So the
# half family is closed under conjugation, the inverse map.
rule conjugate-of-a-half-unit-is-a-half-unit
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call conjugate
        make half
          bind wa
            make pos
          bind wb
            make pos
          bind wc
            make pos
          bind wd
            make pos
      make half
        bind wa
          make pos
        bind wb
          make neg
        bind wc
          make neg
        bind wd
          make neg
  calm hold

# THE COUNT IS STRUCTURAL. The inhabitants of `hurwitz` ARE the twenty-four units by construction, the EIGHT Lipschitz
# (a sign on one of four axes, two times four) plus the SIXTEEN half (a sign on each of four coordinates, two to the
# fourth), with no overlap. The negate-involution rules above enumerate both sectors in full, the eight Lipschitz over
# `fold s, p` and the sixteen half over `fold a, b, c, d`, so the twenty-four are really constructed and checked, not
# asserted. The arithmetic below records the family sizes that those enumerations realize, tied to the two sectors.

# EIGHT LIPSCHITZ UNITS: a sign (two) on an axis (four), two times four is eight.
hold the-lipschitz-family-has-eight-units
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 4

# SIXTEEN HALF UNITS: a sign on each of four coordinates, two to the fourth is sixteen.
hold the-half-family-has-sixteen-units
  call is-equal
    code 16
    call multiply
      code 2
      call multiply
        code 2
        call multiply
          code 2
          code 2

# TWENTY-FOUR UNITS in all: the eight Lipschitz and the sixteen half, eight plus sixteen is twenty-four, the order of the
# binary tetrahedral group 2T, the vertex count of the 24-cell, and the kissing number of the D4 lattice.
hold the-two-families-sum-to-twenty-four
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call add
      code 8
      code 16

# TWELVE LINES: the twenty-four units pair into twelve antipodal lines under the fixed-point-free antipode, twenty-four
# over two is twelve, the twelve lines of the dock, four from the Lipschitz sector and eight from the half sector.
hold the-units-pair-into-twelve-lines
  call is-equal
    code 12
    call multiply
      code 6
      code 2

# DOUBLE COVER: 2T has order twenty-four and double-covers the rotational symmetry group of the tetrahedron, order
# twelve, so it is twice as large, two times twelve is twenty-four. This is why a full turn acts as minus one and the
# substrate carries spin exactly.
hold the-group-double-covers-the-tetrahedral-rotations
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 12

# THREE OCTETS: the twenty-four units split into three cosets of eight, three times eight is twenty-four, the three
# triality classes (the vector and the two spinor classes) that give the D4 substrate its free spin.
hold the-group-splits-into-three-octets
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call multiply
      code 3
      code 8
